Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:38:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AArch64: fix EXT (it indexed the result backwards), add
 CRC32/CRC32C and YIELD

EXT swapped bytes inside each half of the result: a real RNG's ext v,v,v,#8 returned the wrong value (found on Balatro's main by module_validate, 1 function of 150).
CRC32{B,H,W,X} and CRC32C{B,H,W,X} are straight-line code (remill-lift does not finish on a loop in a semantic); YIELD is a hint, like NOP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
